From ee702ba0025b298f75d20376790b194963fc8805 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergio Marin <sergio.marin@pantacor.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 13:44:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] misc: add RDA8810PL mdcom/msys modem command client

The RDA8810PL modem coprocessor owns the PMU rails and the
low-frequency clock gates; the AP requests them over the mdcom mailbox
(dedicated dpram at 0x00200000) with framed msys commands. The RDA5991
combo chip's SDIO core needs the modem-gated 26 MHz reference, which is
why stage 3 (SDIO probe) times out on a modemless boot even though the
always-on I2C slave answers.

Minimal forward-port of the vendor 3.10 md.c + md_sys.c pair:
- SYS channel only (packet framing, magic 0xA8B1), synchronous
  commands only, one in flight;
- probe handshakes with a side-effect-free BP_INFO command and
  disables itself when the bootloader did not start the modem;
- exported helpers for exactly what the combo chip needs:
  v_bt supply (SYS_PM_CMD_EN pm_id 10), aux 26 MHz
  (SYS_GEN_CMD_AUX_CLK) and 32 kHz clock out (SYS_GEN_CMD_CLK_OUT);
- a sysfs cmd attribute for bench experiments
  (echo "pm 10 1" / "aux 1" / "out 1" / "raw <mod> <msg> ...").

Protocol constants and ring semantics verified against the vendor
kernel (arch/arm/plat-rda/) and vendor u-boot (defs_mdcom.h channel
addresses match the kernel layout register for register).

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [local forward-port of vendor protocol]
